    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15221" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁρμάμαξα</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μᾰμ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ης</span>, ἡ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>covered carriage,</i> esp.
			used by Persians; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ξέρξης] μεταβαίνεσκε ἐκ τοῦ ἅρματος
					ἐς ἁρμάμαξαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.41
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				83
			</span></i>; of ambassadors to Susa, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφ᾽ ἁρμαμαξῶν μαλθακῶς κατακείμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					70
				</span></i>
			; used by women, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				3.1.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.4.11
			</span></i>.</div>
